",73,-2,0,"This one is quite confusing to me. Looking at the demo, I don't know which tab will be kept. I think I would remove it. If we had a edit menu when selecting tabs, we could move it there (to close the…"],["9669a7e9_edfac36e",74,-2,0,"I don't remember, do we have a context menu for inactive tabs?"],["bdd93b69_2d46f4c8",75,-2,1,"nit: don't re-use the strings, pull them out as constants or add helper functions and call them here https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/tools/metrics/actions/README.md#don_t-use-the…"],["dedf133f_012df624",72,-2,1,"Nit, the method name is a bit confusing. First time I was kind of expecting the ID to be the one of the tabs to be closed. WDYT: ```suggestion - (void)closeTabsExceptID:(web::WebStateID)itemID; ```"]],0,1381],[7261295,20439,124,2.087,1.667,[[0,1.0,1246,122]],[],0,1382],[7277648,20444,241,4.044,3.245,[[0,1247]],[["8e202281_851a18f2",76,0,1,"Not needed?"],["a0c1e3b4_2eae22cf",77,0,0,"The bug linked here (and in other files) open a completely unrelated bug about a failed flume job…"],["ab74d6a5_e76046f6",78,0,1,"Why is this include here? This header does not appear to need it?"]],0,1383],[7278225,20445,520,9.221,7.387,[[0,1248]],[["04279108_d871019d",79,-1,0,"Why don't you just put that declaration in the header file?"],["1a3d3e17_fd8fa278",80,-1,1,"\"The protocol is usually declared in the same header as the delegating class, as it is part of the API of the class\" go/objc-delegate#heading=h.zedb0g579btl"],["2872711f_70d3b677",81,-1,0,"The Google Objective-C style guide changed, and now explicitly says \"Avoid Forward Declarations\" (go/objc-style#avoid-forward-declarations)."],["8921b4e4_14760591",82,-1,1,"\"Code in initializers and -dealloc should avoid invoking instance methods when possible\". go/objc-style#avoid-messaging-the-current-object-within-initializers-and-dealloc This uses self to call a…"],["95c192fb_ac9c9562",82,-1,0,"This method does not use self, it could be a class method or a static helper function."],["aa631225_ec818020",76,-1,1,"What is this for?"],["bace36a2_7ff3dbb7",78,-1,1,"Please include the header file for the delegate. go/objc-style#avoid-forward-declarations (or inline the delegate definition here)"],["c1708a27_7b39603b",82,-1,1,"I don't understand why this one needs a manual @synthesized. How is it different from _closeButton, which is autosynthesized?"],["fa45d018_4bba47b6",80,-1,1,"Import instead of forward declaration for AssistantSheetViewController (or better, see below, move the delegate declaration into the viewController header)."]],0,1384],[7277652,20445,359,6.365,5.105,[[0,1249]],[["c8c82d79_9011b75e",83,-1,1,"The definition of the instance variable `_viewController` is unnecessary, as synthesize will automatically declare it. This said, if autosynthesize is on, the superclass already has its own unused…"],["2fa00041_f4ae451a",84,0,1,"The same issue is present here, autosynthesis will synthesize a default implementation including an instance variable. Adding a explicit implementation returning nil would be a better approach. As a…"],["cc71a107_09366f29",79,0,0,"You could switch to just get the right class as the rest of the code is identical: ``` - (Class)childCoordinatorClassAccordingToCurrentMode { switch (self.mode) { case AssistantSheetModeAI: return…"]],0,1385],[7303369,20445,8,0.451,0.316,[[0,1250]],[],0,1386],[7303370,20451,187,4.044,3.245,[[0,1.0,1251,189]],[["6b16892f_27afca3a",76,0,1,"I am not sure to understand this. When will it happen?"],["b1cd7763_23678405",76,0,1,"I would move it to somewhere else (more like init or something)."],["e84710e8_8d6cf4e6",1,0,0,"It looks good!"]],0,1387],[7321245,20451,95,2.087,1.667,[[0,1252]],[],0,1388],[7321028,20453,102,2.087,1.667,[[0,1253]],[],0,1389],[7352263,20453,344,6.365,5.105,[[0,1254]],[["29f3bfe0_a878ff45",85,-1,1,"\"Navbar\" is not a word that exist. Per Objective-C guidelines, please use NavigationBar. Or \"Bar\""],["580fd646_05a5257d",82,-1,1,"This is a bit unclear to me. See comment below about remove the \"trailing\" one. Also, I think the \"leading\" should be a \"dynamicLeading\" no?"],["7d7a7a2b_0edb8879",82,-1,1,"(optional) Reading it, this methods seems a bit too complex, but I don't have clear suggestions on how to improve it. Do you think it would be easier if we: 1. Create containers for the…"],["97c4570b_06cd4feb",86,-1,0,"Did you consider using a real UINavigationBar?"],["aed1a0f4_19e3611d",82,-1,1,"Remove"],["b169b923_80497f1d",82,-1,1,"This comment is unclear?"],["e11d96fb_90878142",82,-1,1,"Remove the unnecessary comments"],["f37114de_c105edd3",86,-1,1,"Nit: If the name of the class is `....Button` I am expecting it to be a real UIButton. Could you rename this to `AssistantNavigationBarItem` or similar?"]],0,1390],[7368539,20453,23,0.634,0.471,[[0,1255]],[],0,1391]]}